const items=[{"path":"C:/Users/alexa/simulation/README.md","expected":"# Architecture Evolution Simulator — Start Here / Handoff\n\n## Текущий результат и входные документы\n\nИнтерактивный исследовательский симулятор показывает, как меняются приложение, архитектура, реализация и работа при изменении потребностей. Это подготовленное сравнение допустимых архитектур с объяснениями и evidence.\n\nЧитайте:\n1. [SC-001@v5-candidate](SC-001_desired_architecture_simulator_scenario_v5_candidate.md): цель и желаемый пользовательский путь.\n2. [V3A r10 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r10_pt006_remediation.md): текущая поправка для PT-006; наследует [r9 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r9_delta.md) и исторический [r7](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r7.md).\n3. [PT-006: состав и журнал исправлений](prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md): принятый объём, порядок, критерии и фактический статус.\n4. [PT-006 README](prototypes/PT-006/workspace-shell/README.md) и [полный review](prototypes/PT-006/workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md).\n5. [Индекс прототипов](prototypes/README.md): исторические проверки и ограничения.\n\n## Предметная модель\n\n- Actual Events задают фактический момент. Requirements, CURRENT, файлы, работа и доступный Plan показываются в контексте этого момента.\n- Requirement Model остаётся ненормализованной. Feature/BusinessRule не становятся обязательной общей онтологией.\n- Один Plan / PlanRevision содержит Evolution Steps и другую плановую работу, возможные события, условия, сроки, прогнозы и Planned Change Axes.\n- Evolution Step меняет функцию или реализацию. Он имеет полный target ArchitectureSnapshot и отдельный EvolutionImpact. Работа без такого изменения не обязана быть Step.\n- У PlanRevision есть неизменяемый фактический BASE. Выбор Step или архивного Plan не исполняет работу и не меняет CURRENT.\n- Плановое ожидание маршрута, оценка завершения, обещанный срок и фактический исход — разные утверждения с источниками.\n- Planned Change Axes относятся к ожидаемым изменениям. Actual Hot Paths относятся к выполненной работе.\n- Implementation — вымышленное фактическое дерево файлов плюс отдельные плановые эффекты.\n- A/B имеют общий старт и одинаковые независимые внешние события. Различия последствий имеют авторское объяснение. Нет обязательного победителя или скрытого общего балла.\n\n## Текущий статус и история\n\nSC-001@v5 и полная V3A composition — candidate. Пользователь разрешил ограниченную итерацию исправлений PT-006 по P6R-PR-01A и P6R-PR-02–06. Это отдельное решение исполнения, не принятие всех candidate схем и FR.\n\nДо новой реализации PT-006 имеет 18 видов, content-v5 и подготовленный архив. Review подтвердил пробелы материала и ошибки исторических проекций, хотя 60 тестов/build/lint проходили. Итог новой итерации записывается в журнал PT-006 после проверки.\n\nИсторические r3–r9 и SC-001 v4 сохранены. Старое отдельное Evolution Map и обязательные Evolution Options не являются текущей моделью. PT-001/002/003 сохраняют свои исторические границы; PT-003 не утверждён как удобный интерфейс и не имеет VE promotion. PT-005 не изменяется этой итерацией.\n\nВ старом плане V2 назван committed baseline, но его отдельный файл не найден в проверенном checkout. Не изображайте его независимо восстановленным.\n\n## Работа следующего исполнителя\n\nЧитайте текущие входные документы и журнал исправлений. Не используйте старый review как статус после новых изменений. Не повышайте пример или технический Git commit до User Need, FR или semantic commit. Новую материальную поправку к плану сохраняйте отдельной версией.\n\nРаботайте на локальном snapshot/workspace. Через выбранный пользователем Туннель получайте authoritative HOST, перед переносом проверяйте конфликты, сохраняйте затрагиваемые оригиналы и проверяйте CLI/tests. Не используйте другой Remote Desktop Commander и не автоматизируйте пользовательский Windows desktop без явного разрешения.\n","content":"# Architecture Evolution Simulator — Start Here / Handoff\n\n## Текущий результат и входные документы\n\nИнтерактивный исследовательский симулятор показывает, как меняются приложение, архитектура, реализация и работа при изменении потребностей. Это подготовленное сравнение допустимых архитектур с объяснениями и evidence.\n\nЧитайте:\n1. [SC-001@v5-candidate](SC-001_desired_architecture_simulator_scenario_v5_candidate.md): цель и желаемый пользовательский путь.\n2. [V3A r10 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r10_pt006_remediation.md): текущая поправка для PT-006; наследует [r9 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r9_delta.md) и исторический [r7](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r7.md).\n3. [PT-006: состав и журнал исправлений](prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md): принятый объём, порядок, критерии и фактический статус.\n4. [PT-006 README](prototypes/PT-006/workspace-shell/README.md) и [полный review](prototypes/PT-006/workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md).\n5. [Индекс прототипов](prototypes/README.md): исторические проверки и ограничения.\n\n## Предметная модель\n\n- Actual Events задают фактический момент. Requirements, CURRENT, файлы, работа и доступный Plan показываются в контексте этого момента.\n- Requirement Model остаётся ненормализованной. Feature/BusinessRule не становятся обязательной общей онтологией.\n- Один Plan / PlanRevision содержит Evolution Steps и другую плановую работу, возможные события, условия, сроки, прогнозы и Planned Change Axes.\n- Evolution Step меняет функцию или реализацию. Он имеет полный target ArchitectureSnapshot и отдельный EvolutionImpact. Работа без такого изменения не обязана быть Step.\n- У PlanRevision есть неизменяемый фактический BASE. Выбор Step или архивного Plan не исполняет работу и не меняет CURRENT.\n- Плановое ожидание маршрута, оценка завершения, обещанный срок и фактический исход — разные утверждения с источниками.\n- Planned Change Axes относятся к ожидаемым изменениям. Actual Hot Paths относятся к выполненной работе.\n- Implementation — вымышленное фактическое дерево файлов плюс отдельные плановые эффекты.\n- A/B имеют общий старт и одинаковые независимые внешние события. Различия последствий имеют авторское объяснение. Нет обязательного победителя или скрытого общего балла.\n\n## Текущий статус и история\n\nSC-001@v5 и полная V3A composition — candidate. Пользователь разрешил ограниченную итерацию исправлений PT-006 по P6R-PR-01A и P6R-PR-02–06. Это отдельное решение исполнения, не принятие всех candidate схем и FR.\n\nPT-006 обновлён до content-v6. В текущих 18 видах есть оставшийся материал review и исправленная история. На HOST прошли 71 тест, build и lint. Проверены 144 поверхности каталога, 9 исторических срезов и миграция; финальные правки проверены точечно. Результаты и ограничения находятся в журнале PT-006.\n\n[Полный review](prototypes/PT-006/workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md) описывает версию до исправлений и сохранён как история. Пользовательская проверка удобства, missing V2 и исходная переписка остаются ограничениями. Общие термины: [GLOSSARY](GLOSSARY.md).\n\nИсторические r3–r9 и SC-001 v4 сохранены. Старое отдельное Evolution Map и обязательные Evolution Options не являются текущей моделью. PT-001/002/003 сохраняют свои исторические границы; PT-003 не утверждён как удобный интерфейс и не имеет VE promotion. PT-005 не изменяется этой итерацией.\n\nВ старом плане V2 назван committed baseline, но его отдельный файл не найден в проверенном checkout. Не изображайте его независимо восстановленным.\n\n## Работа следующего исполнителя\n\nЧитайте текущие входные документы и журнал исправлений. Не используйте старый review как статус после новых изменений. Не повышайте пример или технический Git commit до User Need, FR или semantic commit. Новую материальную поправку к плану сохраняйте отдельной версией.\n\nРаботайте на локальном snapshot/workspace. Через выбранный пользователем Туннель получайте authoritative HOST, перед переносом проверяйте конфликты, сохраняйте затрагиваемые оригиналы и проверяйте CLI/tests. Не используйте другой Remote Desktop Commander и не автоматизируйте пользовательский Windows desktop без явного разрешения.\n"},{"path":"C:/Users/alexa/simulation/SC-001_desired_architecture_simulator_scenario_v5_candidate.md","expected":"# SC-001 — Architecture Evolution Simulator: Desired User Scenario\n\n**Version:** `SC-001@v5-candidate` (`REVISED_FROM SC-001@v4-candidate`; v3/v2/v1/v0 retained as historical candidates).  \n**Status:** `CANDIDATE / TRANSACTION OPEN`; this records accepted *user directions*, not semantic commit of the full composition.  \n**Source/provenance:** User clarifications through the accepted Evolution Fitness clarification, R14 follow-up on one Plan and PT staging, R13 candidate correction, earlier R12/R11/R10/R9, `SC-001@v3-candidate`, and historical `V3A-candidate-r7`. Details labelled **candidate design interpretation** are not user-approved schema/FRs.  \n**Scope:** intended prepared research/comparison simulator. Possible future planning assistant for a concrete user's application is **deferred product direction**, not a present requirement.  \n**Not a new r7 revision:** historical `architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r7.md` is unchanged; this file is an independently versioned Desired Scenario candidate.\n\n## 1. Desired Need and current use mode\n\nI want to explore prepared simulations of how a changing application and the work of evolving it unfold under different legitimate architectures, and understand why those architectures have different costs, schedules, available options, implementation consequences and follow-on business/product outcomes. The tool should make actual history, requirement knowledge, architecture/implementation state, planning, contingent futures and work quality inspectable without a hidden universal winner.\n\n**User-confirmed current scope:** Simulation authors script the case: initial application needs, architecture alternatives, shared and branch-specific events, plausible causal effects, implementation and planning histories. An end user primarily **observes, navigates, explains and compares** the prepared alternatives; they are not required to author new architectures or dynamically simulate unprepared outcomes. Branching and conditional plans are still useful inside scripted material. Interactive architecture planning for a particular real application may come later; no IDE, architecture editor, Monte Carlo or real-code generation is presently entailed.\n\n## 2. Truth boundaries and comparison\n\n1. **Shared scenario backbone, causal divergence.** Compared architectures begin at **one shared development starting point** with the same independent situation, externally provided needs and constraints; **situational/exogenous events that do not depend on architectural choice remain the same** for compared architectures. Scripted branch outcomes may diverge where prior architecture, implementation readiness, duration, business opportunity or other explained state causally affects what happens next. An author must not give favorable or unfavorable architecture-independent events to just one compared architecture. Differences in later facts must trace to architectural implementation, work/readiness/timing or downstream causal effects, not arbitrary alternative external scripts. Fair comparison does **not** mean every later event or requirement is identical.\n2. **One fictional calendar may be used.** Simulation dates/times and durations make parallel histories readable. Event order/causal dependency, elapsed time and a calendar timestamp are distinct dimensions; invented durations and estimates are scenario assumptions, not empirically proven universal architecture performance.\n3. **Factual vs planned truth.** Actual Event History records what happened, when and to which compared architecture/branch. Requirement knowledge, factual architecture and fake implementation are reconstructed at the relevant factual cursor. A planned Evolution Step, anticipated event or deadline is **not** itself an Actual Event of execution/completion. Only a later actual outcome establishes actual completion, lateness, customer loss, etc.\n4. **No hindsight.** The *simulation author* can know all scripted futures; the *fictional team at planning time* can use only information then known, expected, forecast, or expressed as uncertainty. An unexpected future event must not be secretly encoded as a known detailed plan; generic contingency/reserve can be planned. Historical plan revisions preserve forecasts and their grounds, including conditional Steps and Planned Change Axes. The author knowing scripted outcomes does not give the fictional team hindsight.\n5. **Branches may accumulate different known requirements.** Shared initial/externally supplied requirements are comparable across architectures. Requirements revealed through genuinely different branch outcomes need not appear in both branch-local factual models. `CDC-10@r6` must be qualified, not silently erased. The existing non-normalized requirement occurrence rule remains.\n\n**Illustrative prepared scenario (not a mandatory domain fixture):** Both branches hear about a potential enterprise contract on April 1. A has delivered an enterprise capability; B is still migrating. A signs and receives new onboarding requirements; B misses the opportunity and replans. All outcomes are predetermined in the demonstration, with inspectable explanations; the fictional team could not know which outcome would occur ahead of time.\n\n## 3. One Plan: user-accepted semantic boundary\n\n**User decision (accepted): there is NO separate Evolution Map object.** The single plan for system development, referred to here as **Plan / PlanRevision** (working name, not a frozen API/schema), contains planned Evolution Steps alongside other planned work, anticipated/possible events, conditions, timing, deadlines, branches, forecasts and preparedness. The historical `EvolutionMapRevision` and stand-alone Evolution Map from r7/R11 are **legacy candidate proposals requiring revision**, not a second source of plan truth. A diagram of Step evolution may later be projected from Plan for navigation, but it is NOT a separately stored plan and is not required by this decision.\n\n**Evolution Step (explicit user meaning):** any planned action that **changes or extends application functionality or the implementation/code/realization**, including refactoring, bug fixes, restructuring or migration where applicable. Work without such a change (e.g., negotiation, risk assessment, test-only verification, coordination, external waiting) can exist within the Plan without being mislabeled as an Evolution Step. Planning may group/display work differently, but does not silently convert unrelated activities into changes of realization.\n\n**Preserve r7 semantics unless deliberately revised:** each planned Evolution Step still exposes a **complete target ArchitectureSnapshot after the Step**, not merely a patch, plus distinct EvolutionImpact. Code/implementation changes need not change the architectural structure; an unchanged architecture snapshot does not imply no work, no implementation effect, or no costs. Plan revisions have an immutable factual BASE and immutable plan-defining versions/history of Step schedules, routes, dependencies, expected snapshots and impacts; effective candidate P-/CDC- rules are stated in the companion r9 amendment; exact storage mechanics remain subject to prototype evidence.\n\n### Planned events, predicted requirements and conditional outcomes\n\n- A Plan can contain an **anticipated concrete event** because the fictional team believes it may or will occur and can describe its **expected impact**. That impact can select one of the conditional Evolution Step routes, alter timing/deadlines, induce replanning or, for example, introduce a concrete requirement. Events may be expected, optional, or contingent; their presence in a Plan does not make them factual Actual Events.\n- **Concrete predicted requirement:** an anticipated event's expected result may be a specific possible new requirement. Mark it **forecast/conditional**, not factually known as an actual demand merely because it is in a Plan. Conversely, a future-delivery requirement already explicitly communicated to the team is **known in its historical Requirement Model**, even if work remains planned; use the information-availability rule (FR-8/9/27), not the implementation date.\n- **Planned Change Axes** capture **less-concrete predicted directions of change** and which product/requirement areas are likely to experience future demands, not fabricated detailed future requirements. They can inform preparedness, optional Steps and structure decisions without pretending to know a future specification.\n- **High project dynamism must be retained as first-class scenario context.** When product change is frequent/volatile or relevant new evidence arrives, the team may reconsider which Change Axes matter, how strongly, their time horizons and preparedness. Axes may arise, weaken, intensify, split, be replaced or cease to be relevant across immutable PlanRevisions. Neither a current Axis nor later observed `ActualHotPath` retroactively overwrites the historical forecast; distinguish predicted change direction from actually observed repeated changes.\n- Anticipated events and current evidence can **qualitatively change the relative likelihood of a route** (more/less likely, dominant, uncertain) without precise percentages or automatically resolving the branch. Changed belief is not occurrence. When a condition is factually satisfied, the associated planned route can become applicable but is not thereby executed; execution remains recorded in Actual Event History.\n- **Conditional/optional Evolution Steps** can be expressed as ordinary Steps with `IF` applicability conditions. A single condition can prepare several Steps. A possible change not yet detailed enough to be a Step can remain a forecast/uncertainty note in the Plan; no separate mandatory `EvolutionOption` object or activation workflow is needed for the first validation. Reconsider only if a concrete independent option lifecycle cannot be preserved through Plan revisions, notes and conditional Steps. No generic rules language or probabilistic engine is required.\n\n### Timing, deadlines, fitness and comparison\n\nA Plan can place Steps, other planned activities, expected events and conditions in a fictional calendar or relative schedule; it can carry dependencies, estimates, deadlines and their provenance. **An enduring deadline identity may have a revised target date with immutable history.** Separately, a changed *forecast completion date* is not a rescheduling of an externally fixed deadline; an actual missed deadline is only established by factual history.\n\nFor every material contemplated conditional route, the simulator should preserve route-relative predecessor/target states, applicability and anticipated effects, and show **conditional future Evolution Impacts, Evolution Fitness, feasibility/consistency and preparedness trade-offs**. A route may be more probable but not certain, and the architecture need not be equally optimized for every scenario. No forced single fitness scalar or calibrated probabilities.\n\n**Evolution Fitness — explicit user-grounded meaning:** at a selected *actual or planned state*, or for a *contemplated implementation/code change*, ask whether delivering a specific requirement or following a prepared route would require **awkward, forced, unexpected or costly migrations**, and how the current/proposed state or change **fits the evolution work and Change Axes the team had planned at this historical point**. Viewpoints can be the current system, a local proposed change, a Step result, one conditional Plan route, or actual development examined later. The evaluation must name the requirement/goal, PlanRevision/route and evidentiary basis, separate migration and other cost classes, and distinguish knowingly planned migration from harmful surprise. A divergence from a plan can be justified when the plan is obsolete; Fitness does not automatically reward following obsolete intent or punish rational migration. This is **not a global architecture-quality score**.\n\n**Fair cross-architecture comparison:** one shared point of departure and **the same architecture-independent situational events** (including calendar anchor, relevant demand, opportunity or external deadline). After that, **only causally explained architecture-dependent consequences** may differ, including completion time, business outcomes, later dependent events and new known requirements. Keep the distinct time cursor, scenario event anchor and branch-local factual event cursor concepts inspectable; no arbitrary branch-favoring external event differences.\n\n## 4. Desired Scenario (prepared scripted case, observer/comparator)\n\nThe ten navigation opportunities below form **one nonrecursive demonstration journey**, not ten mandatory screens or mandatory actions in every case. The Stage A prototype tests only the minimal subset identified by §6 of `V3A-candidate-r9-delta`; subsequent stages validate the remaining capabilities without removing them from the intended outcome.\n\n1. **Enter:** choose a prepared case, see a shared development starting point, architecture alternatives, scenario calendar and shared architecture-independent events.\n2. **Inspect factual state:** at a date/common event and selected architecture branch, see only the factual requirement knowledge, architecture, fake file tree and current historical PlanRevision, with non-normalized requirements and event provenance.\n3. **Inspect the Plan:** see its immutable BASE, concrete Steps changing function or code/implementation, other planned work, deadlines, possible events and conditions. Distinguish what the fictional team knew, forecast, considered uncertain or could not know.\n4. **Explore planned event impacts:** an anticipated concrete event can forecast a specific requirement, alter branch choice, trigger an intended response or lead to changed expectations. A generic uncertainty is represented instead by a Planned Change Axis. Neither is an Actual Event until factually observed.\n5. **Observe change dynamics:** under high product dynamism, historical plan revisions may change the set, salience and direction of Planned Change Axes; users can compare earlier predictions with later ActualHotPaths without hindsight.\n6. **Explore contingent trajectories:** choose any prepared main or fallback conditional route, with its planned Steps, possible events, timing, time constraints and qualitative expectation of likelihood. Inspect a full ArchitectureSnapshot and separate EvolutionImpact after every Step on that route.\n7. **Inspect impacts, Fitness and work:** choose a selected factual or planned architecture state or proposed change, inspect whether fulfilling a concrete requirement would force costly/awkward migration and whether it conflicts with later planned Steps/axes on each relevant conditional route; select architecture-native responsibility/file and see earlier and *conditional* later impacts. From one change/goal, examine its associated planned/actual analysis, implementation, testing, migration, coordination, delay and separate cost classes (accepted R10 PR-2), without assuming each is necessarily an Evolution Step.\n8. **Move factual time:** see shared external events, distinct architecture-specific responses, possible deadline misses, branch-dependent requirements and planning/replanning Actual Events. Historical forecasts, PlanRevisions and immutable Step versions do not silently change. A condition becoming true does not auto-complete planned work.\n9. **Compare architectures:** compare their reactions to the same independent external circumstances at common calendar/scenario anchors, and explain readiness, costs, changed probabilities/contingencies, route preparedness, resulting event divergence and requirement differences that have an actual causal explanation.\n10. **Conclude:** explain conditional preferences, uncertainty, trade-offs and evidence without hidden ranking, ungrounded numeric probabilities or hindsight.\n\n**Observable outcome:** a reader can trace common application circumstances → different architecture/implementation → Plans with Step work, possible events and evolving Change Axes → conditional routes / schedules / forecast requirements → factual events and architectural work → explained downstream differences, while keeping forecast and actuality separate.\n\n## 5. Existing N/FR coverage references (not new committed FRs)\n\n- `N-1..N-13`: evolving architecture alternatives, fair causal comparison, changes, uncertainty, actual event history, work quality (`N-12`) and work for a particular change (`N-13`).\n- `FR-1..9`, `FR-11/12`: architecture-neutral, no hindsight, known future knowledge is actionable, transparent/no hidden verdict, fair comparison.\n- **`FR-10`**: separate cost classes; up-front complexity, transition, migration, coordination, schedule/opportunity effects where represented.\n- `FR-13/15`: KEEP is valid and raw impacts are inspectable.\n- **`FR-14`**: deterministic/scripted cases before Monte Carlo.\n- `FR-16..19`: event order and elapsed/calendar time differ, scenario and branch events and mutations distinct.\n- `FR-20..25`: historical states, contextual work dynamics, evidence-backed quality proxies, reversibility and transparent costs.\n- `FR-26..28` remain **candidate in historical r7**: non-normalized requirements, factual knowledge, and factual vs planned truth. `CDC-10@r9` in the accompanying **candidate delta** clarifies branch-local factual truth; this is not a committed FR revision.\n- `P-42/43/44/45/46` and `CDC-12/16/19/20` as worded in historical r7 are **not modified in place by SC-001**. An accompanying **`V3A-candidate-r9-delta`** proposes revised P-/CDC- semantics and lineage, without editing historical r7 or completing semantic commit.\n\n## 6. Top-level Scenario Realization Units (candidate, not storage classes)\n\n| ID | Contribution | Observable success |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SRU-1` Factual timeline/replay | Shared scenario anchors, one independent event backbone and branch-local factual histories with fictional calendar | Exact branch/time selection reproduces known requirements, actual state and available plan without hindsight. |\n| `SRU-2` Requirement understanding | Non-normalized factual knowledge, including causal branch-local requirements and clear concrete forecasts | Actual requirement vs predicted possible requirement is never misrepresented. |\n| `SRU-3` Architecture interpretation | Architecture-native, factual/planned complete snapshots, no universal BRU ontology | Multiple valid organization and reuse approaches are inspectable. |\n| `SRU-4` Single conditional Plan | PlanRevisions with scheduled Evolution Steps, other work, anticipated events, branching, optional Steps, Change Axes, deadlines, immutable BASE/versions | One Plan is the planning truth; each Step has its full target snapshot, impacts and route provenance. |\n| `SRU-5` Implementation projection | Fictional factual project/file tree and expected changes from Steps | Code/implementation changes can be visible even when architecture structure is unchanged. |\n| `SRU-6` Comparative work/evolution evidence | Per-change work journey, separated cost classes, deadlines, likelihood shifts, uncertainty, cross-route Fitness and causal downstream effects | For a selected state/proposed change and specified route, explain forced/awkward/costly migrations **and alignment or conflict with the historical Plan**, plus work/outcomes, with inspectable evidence rather than a hidden universal score. |\n| `SRU-7` Discoverable workbench | Clear factual context, Requirements, Plan, Architecture, Implementation and contextual inspectors | No separate Evolution Map data model or forced GUI tab; common vs branch-specific and predicted vs actual remain clear. |\n\n**Scope/cost:** the full validation campaign (staged in a single PT plan) extends one scripted fixture with shared independent event(s), two architecture reactions, one conditional anticipated event, a specific predicted requirement, at least one change axis whose salience shifts when project dynamism/evidence changes, a deadline revision vs forecast revision distinction, and conditionally impacted Steps. Do not invent numerical probabilities or mandate an automatic simulator/scheduler.\n\n## 7. Status, provenance and unresolved design details\n\n**User-confirmed:** prepared explorer now; later application-specific planner deferred; single shared development starting point and identical architecture-independent events; only causally explained outcome divergence; **one Plan, no separate Evolution Map**; Evolution Steps are changes to function or implementation/code; Plan can also contain other work, possible/expected events and their impacts, predicted concrete requirements, conditional Step routes, optional Steps, qualitative shifts in likely routes, planned time and deadlines, and **mutable-by-revision Planned Change Axes under high project dynamism**; historical knowledge/no-hindsight; conditional cross-route fitness/impacts; **Evolution Fitness as costly/awkward required migration + fit of a selected state/proposed change to historical planned evolution**, not a global score; R10 PR-2 work exploration.\n\n**Candidate technical terminology:** `PlanRevision` is a working name replacing the previous `EvolutionMapRevision` concept. The decision is single-plan semantics, **not** endorsement of an exact class, event grammar, probability engine or Plan schema.\n\n**Still pending (implementation/prototype details, not reopened user decisions):** (a) exact plan/Step/event/forecast provenance links, (b) planned-event impact on Requirement Model vs already-known future requirement, (c) route fork/rejoin and complete target/lineage consistency, (d) relative likelihood language and evidence, (e) branch-scoped factual cursor UI and prototype validation of revised CDC-10, (f) what work grouping looks like, (g) prototype verification of deadline identity/revised promise vs changed estimate, (h) evidence-based presentation of the now-defined Fitness aspects without mandatory numeric formula, (i) prototype acceptance, formal composition review and semantic commitment. None requires a separate stored Evolution Map.\n\n**Governance:** `SC-001@v4-candidate / TRANSACTION OPEN`; neither this saved candidate nor a future Git commit is semantic commit. Earlier r7, R11, PT-003, R9 remain historical and unchanged. No VE promotion or claimed HOST/TUNNEL synchronization. The r9 amendment is the active **candidate interpretation** of revised P-/CDC- sections, not a silent mutation of r7.\n\n## 8. PT-006 remediation — 2026-10-10\n\nThe user authorized implementing the recommendations of the independent PT-006 completeness review, with documentation updated before source changes. The bounded prototype composition is PR-01A + PR-02–06; its execution record is [PT-006 remediation](prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md). This does not commit the full Scenario or the candidate SRU/storage design.\n\nThe current iteration keeps 18 content kinds and places remaining material in existing canonical models: other planned activities; specific forecast requirements; route expectations with grounds; completion forecasts distinct from commitments; an actual late outcome; changing axes; per-goal work, constraints, contextual lenses and cost/time provenance. Scripted values remain authored assumptions. Optional runtime topology, code sketches, exact estimates, scalarization and a general simulation engine are outside this correction.\n\nCURRENT uses the factual cursor context. Step targets use the selected PlanRevision context. Archived knowledge does not depend on edited navigation order. Historical order and all consumed source facts remain inspectable. New material and v6 migration must preserve customized v5 data and archived facts. Reference diagnostics warn about drafts rather than rejecting all incomplete material.\n\nRead [r10 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r10_pt006_remediation.md) for bounded lineage and status. Historical v4, r7 and r9 documents are unchanged.\n","content":"# SC-001 — Architecture Evolution Simulator: Desired User Scenario\n\n**Version:** `SC-001@v5-candidate` (`REVISED_FROM SC-001@v4-candidate`; v3/v2/v1/v0 retained as historical candidates).  \n**Status:** `CANDIDATE / TRANSACTION OPEN`; this records accepted *user directions*, not semantic commit of the full composition.  \n**Source/provenance:** User clarifications through the accepted Evolution Fitness clarification, R14 follow-up on one Plan and PT staging, R13 candidate correction, earlier R12/R11/R10/R9, `SC-001@v3-candidate`, and historical `V3A-candidate-r7`. Details labelled **candidate design interpretation** are not user-approved schema/FRs.  \n**Scope:** intended prepared research/comparison simulator. Possible future planning assistant for a concrete user's application is **deferred product direction**, not a present requirement.  \n**Not a new r7 revision:** historical `architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r7.md` is unchanged; this file is an independently versioned Desired Scenario candidate.\n\n## 1. Desired Need and current use mode\n\nI want to explore prepared simulations of how a changing application and the work of evolving it unfold under different legitimate architectures, and understand why those architectures have different costs, schedules, available options, implementation consequences and follow-on business/product outcomes. The tool should make actual history, requirement knowledge, architecture/implementation state, planning, contingent futures and work quality inspectable without a hidden universal winner.\n\n**User-confirmed current scope:** Simulation authors script the case: initial application needs, architecture alternatives, shared and branch-specific events, plausible causal effects, implementation and planning histories. An end user primarily **observes, navigates, explains and compares** the prepared alternatives; they are not required to author new architectures or dynamically simulate unprepared outcomes. Branching and conditional plans are still useful inside scripted material. Interactive architecture planning for a particular real application may come later; no IDE, architecture editor, Monte Carlo or real-code generation is presently entailed.\n\n## 2. Truth boundaries and comparison\n\n1. **Shared scenario backbone, causal divergence.** Compared architectures begin at **one shared development starting point** with the same independent situation, externally provided needs and constraints; **situational/exogenous events that do not depend on architectural choice remain the same** for compared architectures. Scripted branch outcomes may diverge where prior architecture, implementation readiness, duration, business opportunity or other explained state causally affects what happens next. An author must not give favorable or unfavorable architecture-independent events to just one compared architecture. Differences in later facts must trace to architectural implementation, work/readiness/timing or downstream causal effects, not arbitrary alternative external scripts. Fair comparison does **not** mean every later event or requirement is identical.\n2. **One fictional calendar may be used.** Simulation dates/times and durations make parallel histories readable. Event order/causal dependency, elapsed time and a calendar timestamp are distinct dimensions; invented durations and estimates are scenario assumptions, not empirically proven universal architecture performance.\n3. **Factual vs planned truth.** Actual Event History records what happened, when and to which compared architecture/branch. Requirement knowledge, factual architecture and fake implementation are reconstructed at the relevant factual cursor. A planned Evolution Step, anticipated event or deadline is **not** itself an Actual Event of execution/completion. Only a later actual outcome establishes actual completion, lateness, customer loss, etc.\n4. **No hindsight.** The *simulation author* can know all scripted futures; the *fictional team at planning time* can use only information then known, expected, forecast, or expressed as uncertainty. An unexpected future event must not be secretly encoded as a known detailed plan; generic contingency/reserve can be planned. Historical plan revisions preserve forecasts and their grounds, including conditional Steps and Planned Change Axes. The author knowing scripted outcomes does not give the fictional team hindsight.\n5. **Branches may accumulate different known requirements.** Shared initial/externally supplied requirements are comparable across architectures. Requirements revealed through genuinely different branch outcomes need not appear in both branch-local factual models. `CDC-10@r6` must be qualified, not silently erased. The existing non-normalized requirement occurrence rule remains.\n\n**Illustrative prepared scenario (not a mandatory domain fixture):** Both branches hear about a potential enterprise contract on April 1. A has delivered an enterprise capability; B is still migrating. A signs and receives new onboarding requirements; B misses the opportunity and replans. All outcomes are predetermined in the demonstration, with inspectable explanations; the fictional team could not know which outcome would occur ahead of time.\n\n## 3. One Plan: user-accepted semantic boundary\n\n**User decision (accepted): there is NO separate Evolution Map object.** The single plan for system development, referred to here as **Plan / PlanRevision** (working name, not a frozen API/schema), contains planned Evolution Steps alongside other planned work, anticipated/possible events, conditions, timing, deadlines, branches, forecasts and preparedness. The historical `EvolutionMapRevision` and stand-alone Evolution Map from r7/R11 are **legacy candidate proposals requiring revision**, not a second source of plan truth. A diagram of Step evolution may later be projected from Plan for navigation, but it is NOT a separately stored plan and is not required by this decision.\n\n**Evolution Step (explicit user meaning):** any planned action that **changes or extends application functionality or the implementation/code/realization**, including refactoring, bug fixes, restructuring or migration where applicable. Work without such a change (e.g., negotiation, risk assessment, test-only verification, coordination, external waiting) can exist within the Plan without being mislabeled as an Evolution Step. Planning may group/display work differently, but does not silently convert unrelated activities into changes of realization.\n\n**Preserve r7 semantics unless deliberately revised:** each planned Evolution Step still exposes a **complete target ArchitectureSnapshot after the Step**, not merely a patch, plus distinct EvolutionImpact. Code/implementation changes need not change the architectural structure; an unchanged architecture snapshot does not imply no work, no implementation effect, or no costs. Plan revisions have an immutable factual BASE and immutable plan-defining versions/history of Step schedules, routes, dependencies, expected snapshots and impacts; effective candidate P-/CDC- rules are stated in the companion r9 amendment; exact storage mechanics remain subject to prototype evidence.\n\n### Planned events, predicted requirements and conditional outcomes\n\n- A Plan can contain an **anticipated concrete event** because the fictional team believes it may or will occur and can describe its **expected impact**. That impact can select one of the conditional Evolution Step routes, alter timing/deadlines, induce replanning or, for example, introduce a concrete requirement. Events may be expected, optional, or contingent; their presence in a Plan does not make them factual Actual Events.\n- **Concrete predicted requirement:** an anticipated event's expected result may be a specific possible new requirement. Mark it **forecast/conditional**, not factually known as an actual demand merely because it is in a Plan. Conversely, a future-delivery requirement already explicitly communicated to the team is **known in its historical Requirement Model**, even if work remains planned; use the information-availability rule (FR-8/9/27), not the implementation date.\n- **Planned Change Axes** capture **less-concrete predicted directions of change** and which product/requirement areas are likely to experience future demands, not fabricated detailed future requirements. They can inform preparedness, optional Steps and structure decisions without pretending to know a future specification.\n- **High project dynamism must be retained as first-class scenario context.** When product change is frequent/volatile or relevant new evidence arrives, the team may reconsider which Change Axes matter, how strongly, their time horizons and preparedness. Axes may arise, weaken, intensify, split, be replaced or cease to be relevant across immutable PlanRevisions. Neither a current Axis nor later observed `ActualHotPath` retroactively overwrites the historical forecast; distinguish predicted change direction from actually observed repeated changes.\n- Anticipated events and current evidence can **qualitatively change the relative likelihood of a route** (more/less likely, dominant, uncertain) without precise percentages or automatically resolving the branch. Changed belief is not occurrence. When a condition is factually satisfied, the associated planned route can become applicable but is not thereby executed; execution remains recorded in Actual Event History.\n- **Conditional/optional Evolution Steps** can be expressed as ordinary Steps with `IF` applicability conditions. A single condition can prepare several Steps. A possible change not yet detailed enough to be a Step can remain a forecast/uncertainty note in the Plan; no separate mandatory `EvolutionOption` object or activation workflow is needed for the first validation. Reconsider only if a concrete independent option lifecycle cannot be preserved through Plan revisions, notes and conditional Steps. No generic rules language or probabilistic engine is required.\n\n### Timing, deadlines, fitness and comparison\n\nA Plan can place Steps, other planned activities, expected events and conditions in a fictional calendar or relative schedule; it can carry dependencies, estimates, deadlines and their provenance. **An enduring deadline identity may have a revised target date with immutable history.** Separately, a changed *forecast completion date* is not a rescheduling of an externally fixed deadline; an actual missed deadline is only established by factual history.\n\nFor every material contemplated conditional route, the simulator should preserve route-relative predecessor/target states, applicability and anticipated effects, and show **conditional future Evolution Impacts, Evolution Fitness, feasibility/consistency and preparedness trade-offs**. A route may be more probable but not certain, and the architecture need not be equally optimized for every scenario. No forced single fitness scalar or calibrated probabilities.\n\n**Evolution Fitness — explicit user-grounded meaning:** at a selected *actual or planned state*, or for a *contemplated implementation/code change*, ask whether delivering a specific requirement or following a prepared route would require **awkward, forced, unexpected or costly migrations**, and how the current/proposed state or change **fits the evolution work and Change Axes the team had planned at this historical point**. Viewpoints can be the current system, a local proposed change, a Step result, one conditional Plan route, or actual development examined later. The evaluation must name the requirement/goal, PlanRevision/route and evidentiary basis, separate migration and other cost classes, and distinguish knowingly planned migration from harmful surprise. A divergence from a plan can be justified when the plan is obsolete; Fitness does not automatically reward following obsolete intent or punish rational migration. This is **not a global architecture-quality score**.\n\n**Fair cross-architecture comparison:** one shared point of departure and **the same architecture-independent situational events** (including calendar anchor, relevant demand, opportunity or external deadline). After that, **only causally explained architecture-dependent consequences** may differ, including completion time, business outcomes, later dependent events and new known requirements. Keep the distinct time cursor, scenario event anchor and branch-local factual event cursor concepts inspectable; no arbitrary branch-favoring external event differences.\n\n## 4. Desired Scenario (prepared scripted case, observer/comparator)\n\nThe ten navigation opportunities below form **one nonrecursive demonstration journey**, not ten mandatory screens or mandatory actions in every case. The Stage A prototype tests only the minimal subset identified by §6 of `V3A-candidate-r9-delta`; subsequent stages validate the remaining capabilities without removing them from the intended outcome.\n\n1. **Enter:** choose a prepared case, see a shared development starting point, architecture alternatives, scenario calendar and shared architecture-independent events.\n2. **Inspect factual state:** at a date/common event and selected architecture branch, see only the factual requirement knowledge, architecture, fake file tree and current historical PlanRevision, with non-normalized requirements and event provenance.\n3. **Inspect the Plan:** see its immutable BASE, concrete Steps changing function or code/implementation, other planned work, deadlines, possible events and conditions. Distinguish what the fictional team knew, forecast, considered uncertain or could not know.\n4. **Explore planned event impacts:** an anticipated concrete event can forecast a specific requirement, alter branch choice, trigger an intended response or lead to changed expectations. A generic uncertainty is represented instead by a Planned Change Axis. Neither is an Actual Event until factually observed.\n5. **Observe change dynamics:** under high product dynamism, historical plan revisions may change the set, salience and direction of Planned Change Axes; users can compare earlier predictions with later ActualHotPaths without hindsight.\n6. **Explore contingent trajectories:** choose any prepared main or fallback conditional route, with its planned Steps, possible events, timing, time constraints and qualitative expectation of likelihood. Inspect a full ArchitectureSnapshot and separate EvolutionImpact after every Step on that route.\n7. **Inspect impacts, Fitness and work:** choose a selected factual or planned architecture state or proposed change, inspect whether fulfilling a concrete requirement would force costly/awkward migration and whether it conflicts with later planned Steps/axes on each relevant conditional route; select architecture-native responsibility/file and see earlier and *conditional* later impacts. From one change/goal, examine its associated planned/actual analysis, implementation, testing, migration, coordination, delay and separate cost classes (accepted R10 PR-2), without assuming each is necessarily an Evolution Step.\n8. **Move factual time:** see shared external events, distinct architecture-specific responses, possible deadline misses, branch-dependent requirements and planning/replanning Actual Events. Historical forecasts, PlanRevisions and immutable Step versions do not silently change. A condition becoming true does not auto-complete planned work.\n9. **Compare architectures:** compare their reactions to the same independent external circumstances at common calendar/scenario anchors, and explain readiness, costs, changed probabilities/contingencies, route preparedness, resulting event divergence and requirement differences that have an actual causal explanation.\n10. **Conclude:** explain conditional preferences, uncertainty, trade-offs and evidence without hidden ranking, ungrounded numeric probabilities or hindsight.\n\n**Observable outcome:** a reader can trace common application circumstances → different architecture/implementation → Plans with Step work, possible events and evolving Change Axes → conditional routes / schedules / forecast requirements → factual events and architectural work → explained downstream differences, while keeping forecast and actuality separate.\n\n## 5. Existing N/FR coverage references (not new committed FRs)\n\n- `N-1..N-13`: evolving architecture alternatives, fair causal comparison, changes, uncertainty, actual event history, work quality (`N-12`) and work for a particular change (`N-13`).\n- `FR-1..9`, `FR-11/12`: architecture-neutral, no hindsight, known future knowledge is actionable, transparent/no hidden verdict, fair comparison.\n- **`FR-10`**: separate cost classes; up-front complexity, transition, migration, coordination, schedule/opportunity effects where represented.\n- `FR-13/15`: KEEP is valid and raw impacts are inspectable.\n- **`FR-14`**: deterministic/scripted cases before Monte Carlo.\n- `FR-16..19`: event order and elapsed/calendar time differ, scenario and branch events and mutations distinct.\n- `FR-20..25`: historical states, contextual work dynamics, evidence-backed quality proxies, reversibility and transparent costs.\n- `FR-26..28` remain **candidate in historical r7**: non-normalized requirements, factual knowledge, and factual vs planned truth. `CDC-10@r9` in the accompanying **candidate delta** clarifies branch-local factual truth; this is not a committed FR revision.\n- `P-42/43/44/45/46` and `CDC-12/16/19/20` as worded in historical r7 are **not modified in place by SC-001**. An accompanying **`V3A-candidate-r9-delta`** proposes revised P-/CDC- semantics and lineage, without editing historical r7 or completing semantic commit.\n\n## 6. Top-level Scenario Realization Units (candidate, not storage classes)\n\n| ID | Contribution | Observable success |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SRU-1` Factual timeline/replay | Shared scenario anchors, one independent event backbone and branch-local factual histories with fictional calendar | Exact branch/time selection reproduces known requirements, actual state and available plan without hindsight. |\n| `SRU-2` Requirement understanding | Non-normalized factual knowledge, including causal branch-local requirements and clear concrete forecasts | Actual requirement vs predicted possible requirement is never misrepresented. |\n| `SRU-3` Architecture interpretation | Architecture-native, factual/planned complete snapshots, no universal BRU ontology | Multiple valid organization and reuse approaches are inspectable. |\n| `SRU-4` Single conditional Plan | PlanRevisions with scheduled Evolution Steps, other work, anticipated events, branching, optional Steps, Change Axes, deadlines, immutable BASE/versions | One Plan is the planning truth; each Step has its full target snapshot, impacts and route provenance. |\n| `SRU-5` Implementation projection | Fictional factual project/file tree and expected changes from Steps | Code/implementation changes can be visible even when architecture structure is unchanged. |\n| `SRU-6` Comparative work/evolution evidence | Per-change work journey, separated cost classes, deadlines, likelihood shifts, uncertainty, cross-route Fitness and causal downstream effects | For a selected state/proposed change and specified route, explain forced/awkward/costly migrations **and alignment or conflict with the historical Plan**, plus work/outcomes, with inspectable evidence rather than a hidden universal score. |\n| `SRU-7` Discoverable workbench | Clear factual context, Requirements, Plan, Architecture, Implementation and contextual inspectors | No separate Evolution Map data model or forced GUI tab; common vs branch-specific and predicted vs actual remain clear. |\n\n**Scope/cost:** the full validation campaign (staged in a single PT plan) extends one scripted fixture with shared independent event(s), two architecture reactions, one conditional anticipated event, a specific predicted requirement, at least one change axis whose salience shifts when project dynamism/evidence changes, a deadline revision vs forecast revision distinction, and conditionally impacted Steps. Do not invent numerical probabilities or mandate an automatic simulator/scheduler.\n\n## 7. Status, provenance and unresolved design details\n\n**User-confirmed:** prepared explorer now; later application-specific planner deferred; single shared development starting point and identical architecture-independent events; only causally explained outcome divergence; **one Plan, no separate Evolution Map**; Evolution Steps are changes to function or implementation/code; Plan can also contain other work, possible/expected events and their impacts, predicted concrete requirements, conditional Step routes, optional Steps, qualitative shifts in likely routes, planned time and deadlines, and **mutable-by-revision Planned Change Axes under high project dynamism**; historical knowledge/no-hindsight; conditional cross-route fitness/impacts; **Evolution Fitness as costly/awkward required migration + fit of a selected state/proposed change to historical planned evolution**, not a global score; R10 PR-2 work exploration.\n\n**Candidate technical terminology:** `PlanRevision` is a working name replacing the previous `EvolutionMapRevision` concept. The decision is single-plan semantics, **not** endorsement of an exact class, event grammar, probability engine or Plan schema.\n\n**Still pending (implementation/prototype details, not reopened user decisions):** (a) exact plan/Step/event/forecast provenance links, (b) planned-event impact on Requirement Model vs already-known future requirement, (c) route fork/rejoin and complete target/lineage consistency, (d) relative likelihood language and evidence, (e) branch-scoped factual cursor UI and prototype validation of revised CDC-10, (f) what work grouping looks like, (g) prototype verification of deadline identity/revised promise vs changed estimate, (h) evidence-based presentation of the now-defined Fitness aspects without mandatory numeric formula, (i) prototype acceptance, formal composition review and semantic commitment. None requires a separate stored Evolution Map.\n\n**Governance:** `SC-001@v4-candidate / TRANSACTION OPEN`; neither this saved candidate nor a future Git commit is semantic commit. Earlier r7, R11, PT-003, R9 remain historical and unchanged. No VE promotion or claimed HOST/TUNNEL synchronization. The r9 amendment is the active **candidate interpretation** of revised P-/CDC- sections, not a silent mutation of r7.\n\n## 8. PT-006 remediation — 2026-10-10\n\nThe user authorized implementing the recommendations of the independent PT-006 completeness review, with documentation updated before source changes. The bounded prototype composition is PR-01A + PR-02–06; its execution record is [PT-006 remediation](prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md). This does not commit the full Scenario or the candidate SRU/storage design.\n\nThe current iteration keeps 18 content kinds and places remaining material in existing canonical models: other planned activities; specific forecast requirements; route expectations with grounds; completion forecasts distinct from commitments; an actual late outcome; changing axes; per-goal work, constraints, contextual lenses and cost/time provenance. Scripted values remain authored assumptions. Optional runtime topology, code sketches, exact estimates, scalarization and a general simulation engine are outside this correction.\n\nCURRENT uses the factual cursor context. Step targets use the selected PlanRevision context. Archived knowledge does not depend on edited navigation order. Historical order and all consumed source facts remain inspectable. New material and v6 migration must preserve customized v5 data and archived facts. Reference diagnostics warn about drafts rather than rejecting all incomplete material.\n\nRead [r10 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r10_pt006_remediation.md) for bounded lineage and status. Historical v4, r7 and r9 documents are unchanged.\n\n\n### Delivery note\n\nPT-006 content-v6 remediation is technically completed: 71 HOST tests, build and lint passed; the catalog, nine historical branch/time slices and migration were checked. Remaining material is authored and inspectable in the existing 18 kinds. The execution record contains exact evidence and limitations. This is not full Scenario acceptance or VE promotion. Shared terminology: [GLOSSARY](GLOSSARY.md).\n"},{"path":"C:/Users/alexa/simulation/architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r10_pt006_remediation.md","expected":"# V3A candidate r10 delta — PT-006 remediation\n\nDate: 2026-10-10. Status: CANDIDATE / TRANSACTION OPEN for the full composition.\nREVISED_FROM: [r9 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r9_delta.md).\nScenario: [SC-001@v5-candidate](SC-001_desired_architecture_simulator_scenario_v5_candidate.md).\n\nThis supplement inherits r9 without replacing historical P-/CDC-/QRP records. It records an independently authorized prototype iteration, not a new semantic baseline or a claim that Stage A/B/C has passed.\n\n## Authorized prototype composition\n\nThe user requested implementation of the PT-006 review recommendations and documentation before prototype changes. Local P6R-PR-01A and P6R-PR-02–06 are committed as this iteration's working composition; P6R-PR-01B is rejected for this iteration. Existing review IDs retain their origin. Full canonical execution records, cost trade-offs and acceptance checks are in [PT-006 remediation](prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md).\n\n## Scenario / SRU contribution\n\n- SRU-1/2: historical event knowledge is independent from live navigation edits.\n- SRU-3/4: factual CURRENT and planned targets resolve in distinct snapshot contexts; one Plan retains other activities, conditions, expectations and time statements.\n- SRU-4/6: authored route-relative forecast/commitment and work/constraint examples fill the review's material gaps without a calculation engine.\n- SRU-5/7: source inspection, own trace facts, ordered history and draft reference warnings remain visible in the same 18-kind shell.\n\nNo Need or Fundamental Requirement is inferred anew from a fixture shape. Historical normalization and standalone Evolution Map remain superseded only under the accepted directions already recorded in v4/r9. Topology/sketch, probability engine, IDE and universal architecture ontology remain optional or deferred as before.\n\n## Current / next version\n\nThis correction targets PT-006 content-v6. Delivery is pending; tests/build/lint/browser results must be recorded after implementation. Customized v5/v4/v3 content and layout-v3 must survive. Untouched authored fixtures may receive the updated demonstration; custom histories are not fabricated or rewritten.\n\n## Open evidence\n\nThe original discussion and missing committed V2 have not been independently recovered. No-guide user UX remains untested. Quantity, duration, money and deadline feasibility are unknown unless the illustrative source explicitly states their authored nature. No exact delivery estimate or automatic VE promotion is made.\n","content":"# V3A candidate r10 delta — PT-006 remediation\n\nDate: 2026-10-10. Status: CANDIDATE / TRANSACTION OPEN for the full composition.\nREVISED_FROM: [r9 delta](architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r9_delta.md).\nScenario: [SC-001@v5-candidate](SC-001_desired_architecture_simulator_scenario_v5_candidate.md).\n\nThis supplement inherits r9 without replacing historical P-/CDC-/QRP records. It records an independently authorized prototype iteration, not a new semantic baseline or a claim that Stage A/B/C has passed.\n\n## Authorized prototype composition\n\nThe user requested implementation of the PT-006 review recommendations and documentation before prototype changes. Local P6R-PR-01A and P6R-PR-02–06 are committed as this iteration's working composition; P6R-PR-01B is rejected for this iteration. Existing review IDs retain their origin. Full canonical execution records, cost trade-offs and acceptance checks are in [PT-006 remediation](prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md).\n\n## Scenario / SRU contribution\n\n- SRU-1/2: historical event knowledge is independent from live navigation edits.\n- SRU-3/4: factual CURRENT and planned targets resolve in distinct snapshot contexts; one Plan retains other activities, conditions, expectations and time statements.\n- SRU-4/6: authored route-relative forecast/commitment and work/constraint examples fill the review's material gaps without a calculation engine.\n- SRU-5/7: source inspection, own trace facts, ordered history and draft reference warnings remain visible in the same 18-kind shell.\n\nNo Need or Fundamental Requirement is inferred anew from a fixture shape. Historical normalization and standalone Evolution Map remain superseded only under the accepted directions already recorded in v4/r9. Topology/sketch, probability engine, IDE and universal architecture ontology remain optional or deferred as before.\n\n## Current / next version\n\nThis correction targets PT-006 content-v6. Technical delivery is completed; final HOST tests are 71/71, build/lint passed. Main browser checks covered 144 surfaces and nine historical slices; final supplements covered affected changes and migration under the current key. Exact results are recorded in PT-006 remediation. Customized v5/v4/v3 content and layout-v3 must survive. Untouched authored fixtures may receive the updated demonstration; custom histories are not fabricated or rewritten.\n\n## Open evidence\n\nThe original discussion and missing committed V2 have not been independently recovered. No-guide user UX remains untested. Quantity, duration, money and deadline feasibility are unknown unless the illustrative source explicitly states their authored nature. No exact delivery estimate or automatic VE promotion is made.\n\nShared terminology: [GLOSSARY](GLOSSARY.md). No full candidate composition commit or VE promotion follows from these technical results.\n"},{"path":"C:/Users/alexa/simulation/prototypes/README.md","expected":"# Prototype Validation Track\n\nPrototype artifacts are separate from the canonical Proposal Composition.\n\n## Identity\n\nPrototype plans use `PT-*` IDs. Validated evidence promoted into the canonical plan uses `VE-*` IDs.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\n```text\nplanned -> prepared -> running -> completed -> interpreted\n```\n\nA prototype may also end as `inconclusive`, `invalidated`, or `superseded`.\n\n## Required sections\n\nEvery `PT-*` should state:\n\n1. target Proposals / CDCs / QRP / questions;\n2. propositions being tested;\n3. scope and non-goals;\n4. fixture/scenario assumptions;\n5. variants;\n6. observable evidence;\n7. acceptance / falsification criteria;\n8. execution procedure;\n9. results;\n10. interpretation and limitations;\n11. main-plan impact.\n\n## Promotion rule\n\nA prototype is exploratory evidence, not canonical truth by itself.\n\nDo not promote fixture-specific assumptions, temporary UI choices, mock data, shortcuts or taxonomy into User Needs, Fundamental Requirements or accepted Proposals merely because they appeared in a prototype.\n\nAfter a prototype is completed:\n\n1. preserve the prototype artifact;\n2. classify tested propositions as `supported`, `unsupported`, `mixed`, or `inconclusive`;\n3. add a `VE-*` record to the canonical Proposal Composition;\n4. update affected Proposal / CDC / QRP status explicitly;\n5. create a new candidate revision if the canonical composition changes materially.\n\nIf a materially new semantic question appears while a prototype is running:\n\n1. do not retroactively pretend the old PT always tested it;\n2. preserve the original PT target/version;\n3. create a new `PT-*` with explicit lineage;\n4. state which mechanics/results are inherited versus newly tested;\n5. do not inherit validation merely because the same UI shell or fixture is reused.\n\nFailed and negative prototypes remain preserved.\n\n## Current prototypes\n\n### PT-001 — Event / Entity Walkthrough\n\nValidates the event-centric simulation model against one concrete Booking SaaS walkthrough before event/entity schema freeze.\n\nFiles:\n\n```text\nPT-001_event_entity_walkthrough.md\nPT-001_stage_a_fixture.md\nPT-001_stage_b_branch_events.md\nPT-001_stage_c_ui.md\nPT-001/\n```\n\nCurrent status: `running` — Stage C UI is technically validated and the later time-travel shell experiment improved the event/state interaction, but formal interpretation / VE promotion is still pending.\n\n### PT-002 — Requirement Surface / Feature Model / State Canvas\n\nHistorical semantic experiment for the r5 candidate:\n\n```text\nRequirement Surface\n  -> branch Functional Decomposition / Feature Model\n  -> Current Realization / TeamPlan\n```\n\nPrimary mechanics still useful to later prototypes:\n- branch-specific event identities;\n- canonical mutation ledger;\n- synchronized event/state replay;\n- first-class ScenarioStep / Widget mechanics.\n\nFile:\n\n```text\nPT-002_requirement_surface_feature_model_state_canvas.md\n```\n\nCurrent status: `running / historically bounded` — PT-002-R1 structural remediation and technical checks pass, but its PFR/Feature/Required-Design-Current-Plan semantics are partially superseded by R7/R8. Stage E interpretation was never promoted into `VE-*`; PT-002 must not be treated as validation of PT-003 semantics.\n\n### PT-003 — Requirement Model / Architecture Planning / Evolution Map\n\nValidates the r7 candidate after R7/R8:\n\n```text\nActual Event History\n  -> non-normalized Requirement Model\n  -> factual CURRENT architecture\n\nPlanning Event\n  -> immutable Plan Revision BASE\n  -> immutable Evolution Step versions\n  -> full target Architecture Snapshot per Step\n  -> replanning / Evolution Options\n```\n\nPrimary questions:\n- non-normalized requirement material and occurrence tracing;\n- one Requirement Model at the Actual Event cursor;\n- BRUs as architecture-side behavior responsibilities;\n- CURRENT vs immutable historical BASE;\n- historical requirement knowledge / no hindsight;\n- immutable Step versions + `REVISED_FROM` lineage;\n- non-monotonic full planned snapshots;\n- plan disruption after an unforeseen requirement;\n- Evolution Option trigger -> Planning Event -> concrete Step;\n- whether full target snapshots make Step-version churn understandable or excessive.\n\nFiles:\n\n```text\nPT-003_requirement_architecture_evolution_map.md\nPT-003/app/\n```\n\nCurrent status: `running` — semantic fixture and UI implementation are synchronized to HOST; model invariants, build, lint and production-preview HTTP smoke pass. Human semantic audit remains pending, so no `VE-*` promotion is performed.\n\n### PT-006 — Workspace / content inventory and remediation\n\n18 content kinds in one A/B workspace: factual State, one Plan, full planned architecture, impacts, forecasts, work and inspectors. [README](PT-006/workspace-shell/README.md), [independent review](PT-006/workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md), [current execution record](PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md).\n\nCurrent status: remediation authorized and documented before source edits. PR-01A and PR-02–06 are selected for execution. Existing 60 tests/build/lint passed before remediation, with confirmed content/history gaps; those checks do not validate the new iteration. New results belong in the execution record. SC-001/V3A remain candidate, no Stage A/B/C or VE promotion.\n","content":"# Prototype Validation Track\n\nPrototype artifacts are separate from the canonical Proposal Composition.\n\n## Identity\n\nPrototype plans use `PT-*` IDs. Validated evidence promoted into the canonical plan uses `VE-*` IDs.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\n```text\nplanned -> prepared -> running -> completed -> interpreted\n```\n\nA prototype may also end as `inconclusive`, `invalidated`, or `superseded`.\n\n## Required sections\n\nEvery `PT-*` should state:\n\n1. target Proposals / CDCs / QRP / questions;\n2. propositions being tested;\n3. scope and non-goals;\n4. fixture/scenario assumptions;\n5. variants;\n6. observable evidence;\n7. acceptance / falsification criteria;\n8. execution procedure;\n9. results;\n10. interpretation and limitations;\n11. main-plan impact.\n\n## Promotion rule\n\nA prototype is exploratory evidence, not canonical truth by itself.\n\nDo not promote fixture-specific assumptions, temporary UI choices, mock data, shortcuts or taxonomy into User Needs, Fundamental Requirements or accepted Proposals merely because they appeared in a prototype.\n\nAfter a prototype is completed:\n\n1. preserve the prototype artifact;\n2. classify tested propositions as `supported`, `unsupported`, `mixed`, or `inconclusive`;\n3. add a `VE-*` record to the canonical Proposal Composition;\n4. update affected Proposal / CDC / QRP status explicitly;\n5. create a new candidate revision if the canonical composition changes materially.\n\nIf a materially new semantic question appears while a prototype is running:\n\n1. do not retroactively pretend the old PT always tested it;\n2. preserve the original PT target/version;\n3. create a new `PT-*` with explicit lineage;\n4. state which mechanics/results are inherited versus newly tested;\n5. do not inherit validation merely because the same UI shell or fixture is reused.\n\nFailed and negative prototypes remain preserved.\n\n## Current prototypes\n\n### PT-001 — Event / Entity Walkthrough\n\nValidates the event-centric simulation model against one concrete Booking SaaS walkthrough before event/entity schema freeze.\n\nFiles:\n\n```text\nPT-001_event_entity_walkthrough.md\nPT-001_stage_a_fixture.md\nPT-001_stage_b_branch_events.md\nPT-001_stage_c_ui.md\nPT-001/\n```\n\nCurrent status: `running` — Stage C UI is technically validated and the later time-travel shell experiment improved the event/state interaction, but formal interpretation / VE promotion is still pending.\n\n### PT-002 — Requirement Surface / Feature Model / State Canvas\n\nHistorical semantic experiment for the r5 candidate:\n\n```text\nRequirement Surface\n  -> branch Functional Decomposition / Feature Model\n  -> Current Realization / TeamPlan\n```\n\nPrimary mechanics still useful to later prototypes:\n- branch-specific event identities;\n- canonical mutation ledger;\n- synchronized event/state replay;\n- first-class ScenarioStep / Widget mechanics.\n\nFile:\n\n```text\nPT-002_requirement_surface_feature_model_state_canvas.md\n```\n\nCurrent status: `running / historically bounded` — PT-002-R1 structural remediation and technical checks pass, but its PFR/Feature/Required-Design-Current-Plan semantics are partially superseded by R7/R8. Stage E interpretation was never promoted into `VE-*`; PT-002 must not be treated as validation of PT-003 semantics.\n\n### PT-003 — Requirement Model / Architecture Planning / Evolution Map\n\nValidates the r7 candidate after R7/R8:\n\n```text\nActual Event History\n  -> non-normalized Requirement Model\n  -> factual CURRENT architecture\n\nPlanning Event\n  -> immutable Plan Revision BASE\n  -> immutable Evolution Step versions\n  -> full target Architecture Snapshot per Step\n  -> replanning / Evolution Options\n```\n\nPrimary questions:\n- non-normalized requirement material and occurrence tracing;\n- one Requirement Model at the Actual Event cursor;\n- BRUs as architecture-side behavior responsibilities;\n- CURRENT vs immutable historical BASE;\n- historical requirement knowledge / no hindsight;\n- immutable Step versions + `REVISED_FROM` lineage;\n- non-monotonic full planned snapshots;\n- plan disruption after an unforeseen requirement;\n- Evolution Option trigger -> Planning Event -> concrete Step;\n- whether full target snapshots make Step-version churn understandable or excessive.\n\nFiles:\n\n```text\nPT-003_requirement_architecture_evolution_map.md\nPT-003/app/\n```\n\nCurrent status: `running` — semantic fixture and UI implementation are synchronized to HOST; model invariants, build, lint and production-preview HTTP smoke pass. Human semantic audit remains pending, so no `VE-*` promotion is performed.\n\n### PT-006 — Workspace / content inventory and remediation\n\n18 content kinds in one A/B workspace: factual State, one Plan, full planned architecture, impacts, forecasts, work and inspectors. [README](PT-006/workspace-shell/README.md), [independent review](PT-006/workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md), [current execution record](PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md).\n\nCurrent status: completed technically for the bounded remediation. PR-01A and PR-02–06 are implemented in content-v6. Final HOST checks: 71 tests/build/lint passed; catalog, nine archived branch/time slices, source history, new material and preserved data/layout migration verified. User semantic/UX interpretation and VE promotion remain pending. SC-001/V3A remain candidate; no Stage A/B/C acceptance. See the execution record for current findings status and exact evidence.\n"},{"path":"C:/Users/alexa/simulation/prototypes/PT-006/PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md","expected":"# PT-006: исправления после независимого review\n\nДата: 2026-10-10. Рабочий документ исполнения.\nОснование: просьба пользователя сначала обновить документы, затем изменить прототип по рекомендациям review.\nИсточник: [полный review](workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md), namespace P6R-.\nИсторическая копия для чтения: [GitHub snapshot](https://github.com/AlexPastukhh/forfiles/blob/17c28c22ceab6f9c47b1a5549a7681f37aee2efc/artifacts/2026-10-10/review-pt006-content-143710-386ee743.md).\n\n## Состояние работы\n\nПринята граница изменений прототипа. Документы подготовлены до изменения исходников.\nРеализация и новая проверка ещё не завершены. Результаты предыдущей версии не засчитываются как проверка исправлений.\nSC-001 и полная V3A composition остаются candidate. Принятие этой итерации PT-006 не принимает все их схемы и SRU.\n\n## Принятый состав\n\n| Proposal | Решение этой итерации | Trace |\n|---|---|---|\n| P6R-PR-01A | committed: добавить различимые разделы и авторские примеры в текущие 18 видов | P6R-F-P-01; N-P6R-01; FR-P6R-01 |\n| P6R-PR-01B | rejected для этой итерации: дополнительные виды не требуются | ALTERNATIVE_TO PR-01A; P6R-PG-01 |\n| P6R-PR-02 | committed: раздельное разрешение CURRENT и плановой цели, даже при совпадении ID | P6R-F-P-02; WR-P6R-01 |\n| P6R-PR-03 | committed: архивные знания используют архивные события; полная лента нужна только для навигации | P6R-F-P-03; WR-P6R-02 |\n| P6R-PR-04 | committed: показывать изменение порядка событий и Steps отдельно от полей объектов | P6R-F-P-04 |\n| P6R-PR-05 | committed: показать все реальные источники проекций и собственные trace.links | P6R-F-P-05 |\n| P6R-PR-06 | committed: предупреждать о неразрешённых ссылках; разрешать сохранение черновика | P6R-F-R-01; trigger наступает при расширении материала |\n\nP6R-PG-01: ALTERNATIVE_GROUP, выбран 01A. P6R-PG-02: SOFT_BUNDLE, включены 02–05.\nКомпозиция этой итерации: COMMITTED как рабочая граница по указанию пользователя.\nP6R-F-U-01: resolved для этой итерации через разрешение реализовать рекомендации review. Это не доказательство удобства размещения.\nНет несоблюдённых REQUIRES или одновременных конфликтующих вариантов.\nНовые глобальные Need/FR, расчётный engine и отдельный Evolution Map не добавлены.\n\n## Материал и место хранения\n\n| Остаток review | Каноническое место | Различимый пример |\n|---|---|---|\n| Плановая работа без изменения реализации | Plan.activities | Переговоры, тестовая проверка, координация, ожидание; нет обязательного targetSnapshotRef |\n| Конкретное прогнозное требование | Plan.anticipatedEvents | Потребность в корпоративном онбординге до фактического R-A3; forecast отдельно от Requirement Model |\n| Ожидание маршрута и основания | Plan.routeExpectations | IF CONTRACT / ELSE: качественное ожидание в R1/R2; условие не равно вероятности или выполнению |\n| Оценка завершения и обязательный срок | Plan.completionForecast, deadline | В B меняется оценка; обещание отдельно пересогласовано; есть источник, причина и история |\n| Фактический пропуск срока | Work.deadlineOutcomes / Actual Events | Авторский исход B после прошедшего обещанного срока; плановая дата не объявляется фактом |\n| Динамичность и пересмотр осей | Scenario.context / Plan.changeAxes | Исторические R1/R2 различаются направлением, значимостью, горизонтом и основанием |\n| Работа по цели и constraints | Work.details | Анализ, реализация, тестирование, координация, ожидание, зависимости, compatibility, rollout |\n| Линзы работы и контекста | Work.details / Scenario.context | Откат, изоляция эксперимента, feedback, условия автономии команды и инженерной среды |\n| Происхождение затрат и времени | Work.costFacts | Источник, единица, количество или unknown, основание времени; разовое/повторяющееся обязательство |\n| Fitness разных маршрутов | Fitness.assessments | Оба подготовленных маршрута с конкретной целью и evidence; отдельные классы затрат без общего балла |\n\nВсе примеры — авторские данные вымышленного случая. Нет калиброванных вероятностей, измеренного effort или гарантированных сроков.\nOptional topology/sketch остаются предложениями на будущее: P-47/P-48 не превращены в обязательный scope.\nОдин факт хранится в одном каноническом месте; окно проекции хранит только настройки или явно названные собственные факты.\n\n## Порядок и совместимость\n\n1. Сохранить этот состав и обновить Start Here, SC-001@v5-candidate и r10-delta.\n2. Сделать изменения на отдельной локальной копии свежих исходников.\n3. Перед переносом сверить HOST с прочитанным исходным содержимым и сохранить затрагиваемые оригиналы.\n4. Сохранить пользовательские v5/v4/v3 данные и layout-v3. Использовать content-v6.\n5. Обновить нетронутый подготовленный пример; пользовательские факты и архивы не переписывать материалом нового примера.\n6. Выполнить проверки и дописать результаты в этот документ и README.\n\n## Критерии проверки\n\n- Изменённый фактический CURRENT и старый плановый target с одинаковым ID одновременно показывают разные правильные версии.\n- Перестановка live-событий не меняет знания в архивном A-02. Полная лента остаётся доступна.\n- Неизвестное событие и изменённая идентичность архивного события не получают чужой исторический State.\n- История явно показывает порядок events.records и plan.steps. Неупорядоченные identity-коллекции не создают ложных замен.\n- Impact History и Event / Entity Explorer раскрывают architecture/files; trace-only факт виден, настройка выбора не является событием.\n- Каждый новый материал имеет State, Schema, renderer и сохранённый исторический пример, где это нужно.\n- Новые refs имеют предупреждения; сохранение валидного черновика разрешено.\n- Миграция сохраняет изменённые данные, старые архивы, текущие выборы и геометрию.\n- npm test, build, lint и изолированный браузерный прогон A/B проходят после изменений.\n\n## Затраты и ограничения\n\nКоличественная delta unknown. Deadline и бюджет не установлены.\n01A сохраняет каталог и layout; добавляет форму данных, примеры, историю и разделы внутри окон.\n02–05 требуют небольших отдельных механизмов разрешения контекста и источников.\n06 добавляет диагностику ссылок без запрета неполных черновиков.\nРабочая стоимость просмотра зависит от объёма разделов; пользовательский UX ещё не проверен.\n\n## Review / Execution Log\n\n2026-10-10, до изменений кода: исходный review сохранён; состав выше принят для исполнения.\nP6R-F-P-01–05 остаются подтверждёнными Problems исходной проверенной версии; исправление ещё не подтверждено.\nP6R-F-R-01: act-now, добавляется mitigation PR-06.\nP6R-F-U-01: resolved для выбора состава; отдельная проверка удобства остаётся Evidence Gap.\nEG-P6R-02: исходная переписка и отсутствующий V2 по-прежнему недоступны.\nEG-P6R-03: no-guide UX и время действий пользователя не измерены.\nGitHub reading snapshot не изменяется и не является owner этого рабочего документа.\n","content":"# PT-006: исправления после независимого review\n\nДата: 2026-10-10. Рабочий документ исполнения.\nОснование: просьба пользователя сначала обновить документы, затем изменить прототип по рекомендациям review.\nИсточник: [полный review](workspace-shell/PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md), namespace P6R-.\nИсторическая копия для чтения: [GitHub snapshot](https://github.com/AlexPastukhh/forfiles/blob/17c28c22ceab6f9c47b1a5549a7681f37aee2efc/artifacts/2026-10-10/review-pt006-content-143710-386ee743.md).\n\n## Состояние работы\n\n**Итерация завершена технически.** Документы сохранены до изменений исходников. Принятый состав реализован в content-v6. Последний прогон: 71/71 тест, build и lint прошли. Проверены каталог A/B, история, новые разделы и миграция. Пользовательская проверка удобства ещё не выполнена.\nТермины: [GLOSSARY](../../GLOSSARY.md).\nSC-001 и полная V3A composition остаются candidate. Принятие этой итерации PT-006 не принимает все их схемы и SRU.\n\n## Принятый состав\n\n| Proposal | Решение этой итерации | Trace |\n|---|---|---|\n| P6R-PR-01A | committed: добавить различимые разделы и авторские примеры в текущие 18 видов | P6R-F-P-01; N-P6R-01; FR-P6R-01 |\n| P6R-PR-01B | rejected для этой итерации: дополнительные виды не требуются | ALTERNATIVE_TO PR-01A; P6R-PG-01 |\n| P6R-PR-02 | committed: раздельное разрешение CURRENT и плановой цели, даже при совпадении ID | P6R-F-P-02; WR-P6R-01 |\n| P6R-PR-03 | committed: архивные знания используют архивные события; полная лента нужна только для навигации | P6R-F-P-03; WR-P6R-02 |\n| P6R-PR-04 | committed: показывать изменение порядка событий и Steps отдельно от полей объектов | P6R-F-P-04 |\n| P6R-PR-05 | committed: показать все реальные источники проекций и собственные trace.links | P6R-F-P-05 |\n| P6R-PR-06 | committed: предупреждать о неразрешённых ссылках; разрешать сохранение черновика | P6R-F-R-01; trigger наступает при расширении материала |\n\nP6R-PG-01: ALTERNATIVE_GROUP, выбран 01A. P6R-PG-02: SOFT_BUNDLE, включены 02–05.\nКомпозиция этой итерации: COMMITTED как рабочая граница по указанию пользователя.\nP6R-F-U-01: resolved для этой итерации через разрешение реализовать рекомендации review. Это не доказательство удобства размещения.\nНет несоблюдённых REQUIRES или одновременных конфликтующих вариантов.\nНовые глобальные Need/FR, расчётный engine и отдельный Evolution Map не добавлены.\n\n## Материал и место хранения\n\n| Остаток review | Каноническое место | Различимый пример |\n|---|---|---|\n| Плановая работа без изменения реализации | Plan.activities | Переговоры, тестовая проверка, координация, ожидание; нет обязательного targetSnapshotRef |\n| Конкретное прогнозное требование | Plan.anticipatedEvents | Потребность в корпоративном онбординге до фактического R-A3; forecast отдельно от Requirement Model |\n| Ожидание маршрута и основания | Plan.routeExpectations | IF CONTRACT / ELSE: качественное ожидание в R1/R2; условие не равно вероятности или выполнению |\n| Оценка завершения и обязательный срок | Plan.completionForecast, deadline | В B меняется оценка; обещание отдельно пересогласовано; есть источник, причина и история |\n| Фактический пропуск срока | Work.deadlineOutcomes / Actual Events | Авторский исход B после прошедшего обещанного срока; плановая дата не объявляется фактом |\n| Динамичность и пересмотр осей | Scenario.context / Plan.changeAxes | Исторические R1/R2 различаются направлением, значимостью, горизонтом и основанием |\n| Работа по цели и constraints | Work.details | Анализ, реализация, тестирование, координация, ожидание, зависимости, compatibility, rollout |\n| Линзы работы и контекста | Work.details / Scenario.context | Откат, изоляция эксперимента, feedback, условия автономии команды и инженерной среды |\n| Происхождение затрат и времени | Work.costFacts | Источник, единица, количество или unknown, основание времени; разовое/повторяющееся обязательство |\n| Fitness разных маршрутов | Fitness.assessments | Оба подготовленных маршрута с конкретной целью и evidence; отдельные классы затрат без общего балла |\n\nВсе примеры — авторские данные вымышленного случая. Нет калиброванных вероятностей, измеренного effort или гарантированных сроков.\nOptional topology/sketch остаются предложениями на будущее: P-47/P-48 не превращены в обязательный scope.\nОдин факт хранится в одном каноническом месте; окно проекции хранит только настройки или явно названные собственные факты.\n\n## Порядок и совместимость\n\n1. Сохранить этот состав и обновить Start Here, SC-001@v5-candidate и r10-delta.\n2. Сделать изменения на отдельной локальной копии свежих исходников.\n3. Перед переносом сверить HOST с прочитанным исходным содержимым и сохранить затрагиваемые оригиналы.\n4. Сохранить пользовательские v5/v4/v3 данные и layout-v3. Использовать content-v6.\n5. Обновить нетронутый подготовленный пример; пользовательские факты и архивы не переписывать материалом нового примера.\n6. Выполнить проверки и дописать результаты в этот документ и README.\n\n## Критерии проверки\n\n- Изменённый фактический CURRENT и старый плановый target с одинаковым ID одновременно показывают разные правильные версии.\n- Перестановка live-событий не меняет знания в архивном A-02. Полная лента остаётся доступна.\n- Неизвестное событие и изменённая идентичность архивного события не получают чужой исторический State.\n- История явно показывает порядок events.records и plan.steps. Неупорядоченные identity-коллекции не создают ложных замен.\n- Impact History и Event / Entity Explorer раскрывают architecture/files; trace-only факт виден, настройка выбора не является событием.\n- Каждый новый материал имеет State, Schema, renderer и сохранённый исторический пример, где это нужно.\n- Новые refs имеют предупреждения; сохранение валидного черновика разрешено.\n- Миграция сохраняет изменённые данные, старые архивы, текущие выборы и геометрию.\n- npm test, build, lint и изолированный браузерный прогон A/B проходят после изменений.\n\n## Затраты и ограничения\n\nКоличественная delta unknown. Deadline и бюджет не установлены.\n01A сохраняет каталог и layout; добавляет форму данных, примеры, историю и разделы внутри окон.\n02–05 требуют небольших отдельных механизмов разрешения контекста и источников.\n06 добавляет диагностику ссылок без запрета неполных черновиков.\nРабочая стоимость просмотра зависит от объёма разделов; пользовательский UX ещё не проверен.\n\n## Review / Execution Log\n\n2026-10-10, до изменений кода: исходный review сохранён; состав выше принят для исполнения.\nP6R-F-P-01–05 остаются подтверждёнными Problems исходной проверенной версии; исправление ещё не подтверждено.\nP6R-F-R-01: act-now, добавляется mitigation PR-06.\nP6R-F-U-01: resolved для выбора состава; отдельная проверка удобства остаётся Evidence Gap.\nEG-P6R-02: исходная переписка и отсутствующий V2 по-прежнему недоступны.\nEG-P6R-03: no-guide UX и время действий пользователя не измерены.\nGitHub reading snapshot не изменяется и не является owner этого рабочего документа.\n\n## Реализация и проверка после изменений\n\n| Предмет | Фактический результат |\n|---|---|\n| P6R-PR-01A | Материал размещён в существующих 18 видах. Есть State, Schema, renderer и исторические авторские примеры |\n| P6R-PR-02 | resolveSnapshot различает actual/planned; CURRENT и старый target с одним ID сохраняют разные payload |\n| P6R-PR-03 | Архивный event prefix отделён от navigationEvents; старое знание не зависит от live-порядка |\n| P6R-PR-04 | reorder виден для events.records, plan.steps, plan.activities; identity diff не заменяет неизменённые объекты |\n| P6R-PR-05 | Impact History / Explorer читают architecture/files; History Trace учитывает собственные links |\n| P6R-PR-06 | Предупреждения о missing targets, impacts, маршрутах, связях, файлах, источниках знания и эпизодах; черновик сохраняется |\n| Совместимость | v5/v4/v3 и layout-v3 сохранены. Нетронутый пример обновляется; изменённые факты и архивы остаются пользовательскими |\n| Старый payload под ключом v6 | Проверен на двух загрузках без legacy fallback; пример обновляется, custom State/архив сохраняется |\n| npm test на HOST | **71/71, exit 0**: content 17, history 13, remediation 11, workspace 26, drag 4 |\n| npm run build | **exit 0**, TypeScript + Vite 8.3.3 |\n| npm run lint | **0 warnings / 0 errors, exit 0** |\n| Каталог | Основной прогон: 144 сочетания = 2 ветки × 18 видов × 4 режима; State/Schema читаются |\n| Исторические срезы | 9 срезов: 4 A, 5 B; точные файлы, известные требования, PlanRevision и read-only |\n| Final UI supplements | Точечные проверки после последних правок: один ID в разных контекстах, предупреждение, новые разделы, primary-key migration |\n| Browser runtime | В трёх завершённых прогонах исключений приложения не зарегистрировано |\n| Visual QA | Снимки прогноз/обязательство, условий работы, cost provenance и предупреждения просмотрены; в проверенных секциях нет горизонтального переполнения |\n\nПри первой сборке возникла ошибка TypeScript о возможном undefined snapshot. Условие renderer исправлено; последующие сборки прошли.\nНа локальной копии не было React/TypeScript-зависимостей. Полные подтверждённые тесты и сборка выполнены на HOST с его установленными зависимостями.\n\n### Совместимость и смысл примера\n\nДобавлен B-05, 16 мая: подготовленный фактический исход пропуска обещанного срока 15 мая. Ранее, в B-04, такого факта нет. Оценка завершения 18 мая не изменяла обязательство автоматически. Это авторское обещание готовности в данном случае, отдельно от условия коммерческого договора.\n\nУ custom v5-данных новый авторский материал не вставляется в изменённые факты и архивы. Если новый раздел отсутствует, UI сообщает, что он не задан. Нетронутый пример получает материал автоматически. Выборы, старые storage keys и геометрия остаются.\n\nПовторное восстановление уже подготовленного v6 State не меняет его данные и imported flag. Отдельно проверен старый v5 payload под текущим v6 key — возможный результат горячего обновления. Само горячее обновление пользовательского профиля не автоматизировалось.\n\n### Доказательства и границы\n\nHOST: remediation-evidence-20261010/ui-results.json, visual-results.json, current-key-results.json и PNG.\nПрогоны: remediation-ui-qa-20261010.cjs, remediation-ui-visual-20261010.cjs, remediation-ui-primary-key-20261010.cjs.\nОригиналы: remediation-backups/2026-10-10-docs-first и /2026-10-10-source-before; следующие точечные версии сохранены отдельно.\n\nВсе проверки браузера выполнены в отдельных временных профилях. Пользовательский браузерный профиль не изменён.\nОсновная матрица UI выполнена до финальной диагностики/восстановления; затронутые части проверены отдельными прогонами после этих правок. Матрица не выдается за повторные 144 сценария последней версии.\n\nИсходный review и его GitHub snapshot сохранены неизменёнными. Ни полный Scenario, ни candidate V3A composition, ни Stage A/B/C, ни VE автоматически не приняты. Полный replay/численный engine не реализован этой итерацией. EG-P6R-02 и EG-P6R-03 остаются открытыми.\n\n### Review / Execution Log — завершение\n\n- Target: PT-006, content-v6, history.version = 1; исходники определены SHA-256 ниже.\n- P6R-F-P-01: resolved в пределах доступного материала и подготовленного случая через PR-01A; исходная переписка ограничивает более широкую гарантию «все планы без остатка».\n- P6R-F-P-02/03: resolved; совпадение ID и live reorder проверены в моделях и UI.\n- P6R-F-P-04/05: resolved для объявленного порядка, источников и собственных trace facts; counterexamples проверены.\n- P6R-F-R-01: mitigated через PR-06; общая ссылочная целостность и полнота произвольного случая не гарантированы.\n- P6R-F-U-01: resolved для выбранной композиции 01A; независимые окна/merge остаются последующим UX-решением.\n- PR-01A + PR-02–06: committed и реализованы в этой итерации. PR-01B rejected для неё. PG-01/02 сохраняют указанные выше relations.\n- EG-P6R-02: original discussion / missing V2 unavailable. EG-P6R-03: no-guide UX и время действий не измерены.\n- Optional P-47/P-48, engines, numeric calibration: вне текущей коррекции; revisit при конкретной пользе/новом scope.\n- Новых blocking questions нет. User Assistance не требуется для уже выполненных исправлений.\n- Следующий шаг: открыть новые разделы и оценить их размещение перед объединением окон.\n- Git commit в рабочем репозитории не создавался. Принятие композиции и Git commit — разные действия.\n\n## Точная проверенная версия\n\n| Файл | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| src/AdditionalContent.tsx | 6ff8a6e1b193fa56ffbb9b03aebec5da5d83695de386472795ebc56c69eb25f7 |\n| src/App.tsx | aafe2ec12cc8d7f3955a6913de1ac2b610b41728fd648c3a7103c0d7b937c9d8 |\n| src/DomainContent.tsx | 6681d3347a586f022375eb5e5b664f6df7401626682a86dbb337ba6227fdd79b |\n| src/HistoryContent.tsx | a9fc1dcaf127758f15e245c0a66a9906996929b107ac8d7a0b79d12dc71bdfc8 |\n| src/MaterialContent.tsx | 349584e7adacc31bce47d9b3cf03a7e6a28d4af3df4bdd52d035c7a517a66c05 |\n| src/content.ts | a49edc79ce5498660e2c050da81586778c66dd6e8d814a65415eee09735d6a62 |\n| src/extraContent.ts | b7c5cae7cc78d474695824212fce602d0602c9180c06fd9e754d65c3c410b066 |\n| src/history.ts | 6b5ad45f1553c4a5c023034c0605ea4b868b55db4f8354d19b4ec8e7dffb681d |\n| src/main.tsx | 870e4f68c1617393a0abbc76b6213bf76665ed4980bf08ed1e8fe497925786f5 |\n| src/material.ts | 720272fccfe0cb9ee4ddb6c44b2907ed637c9149a8053166d8009973b8173983 |\n| src/references.ts | 2d86c9e2c8e1b54be16c86e21929c287910ab3bece1574e7972282327422f1bd |\n| src/styles.css | 64e9c7d52c0fa323f1884105223705d6a6d8b1a667d63c6790d2fd9313ff23dc |\n| src/windowDrag.ts | 7cba7fbecbd9b04b70da626cc1bf2043631433ba092fc7aaa9baaa05f32c82d9 |\n| src/workspace.ts | 6a6084afa2d5d89b194512a623e2fdb411d596ff3980a5f27a04846505c2e7e1 |\n"},{"path":"C:/Users/alexa/simulation/prototypes/PT-006/workspace-shell/README.md","expected":"# PT-006 · Architecture Simulator Workspace — content inventory prototype\n\n**Current iteration:** documentation prepared before source changes; implementation of P6R-PR-01A and P6R-PR-02–06 is authorized. See [working remediation record](../PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md). New results are pending; verification below describes the preceding version.\n\n**Status:** working UI prototype, not simulation engine or semantically committed product model. Built against the `SC-001@v5-candidate` and `V3A-candidate-r10-delta` interpretation, plus the earlier Workspace discussions. Candidate documents and the in-app fixture are not promoted to a committed baseline.\n\n## Launch and verify (Windows)\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\alexa\\simulation\\prototypes\\PT-006\\workspace-shell\nnpm run dev -- --port 4196 --strictPort\nnpm test\nnpm run build\nnpm run lint\n```\n\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:4196/ .\n\n## All 18 window content types\n\n| Content type | Role |\n|---|---|\n| Scenario / Context | Same initial app, shared constraints and exogenous scenario anchor |\n| Actual Events | Branch-local factual events and selected factual cursor |\n| Current State | Factual Requirements / Architecture CURRENT / files at the selected archived event |\n| Requirement Model | Factually known, intentionally non-normalized requirements at selected event cursor |\n| Architecture | Existing compact combined diagram/snapshot preview, retained for later merge decision |\n| Architecture Planning | Complete planned target ArchitectureSnapshot for the selected conditional Step |\n| Plan | One PlanRevision: BASE, conditional Steps, deadlines, forecasts, axes and intended implementation effects |\n| Forecasts / Deadlines | Projected event/demand and conditional route selection, not factual events |\n| Planned Change Axes | Future-facing expected directions, separate from actual hot paths |\n| Actual Hot Paths | Observed repeated changes, separate from forecast axes |\n| Evolution Impact | Per-Step/route architecture/file impact, not a full snapshot |\n| Impact History / Future | Actual CURRENT/file changes from archived transitions plus route-qualified planned future impacts |\n| Evolution Fitness | Migration, plan alignment, separate costs and cited fixture evidence, no hidden scalar |\n| Implementation / Files | Event-linked actual file tree, earlier versions and separate planned file effects |\n| Requirement / Implementation Trace | Requirement–architecture–file links; trace projection does not normalize requirements |\n| Event / Entity Explorer | Event → newly known requirements and before/after State changes |\n| Cross-Architecture Comparison | Same shared event and branch-specific consequences in text; not two architecture diagrams side-by-side |\n| Work Dynamics / Hot Paths | Work episodes and hot-path evidence, retained combined for possible future split/merge |\n\nAll content types have an independent `State` slice and possible `JSON Schema` exposed via the global header inspector or panel-edge buttons, whether or not an instance is on-screen. **For projection types** (such as Forecasts, Current State or Impact History), their own editable State describes selection/view settings, while the same inspector also exposes expandable **canonical source State and JSON Schemas** for all underlying data rendered in the view. This avoids copying Plan or Events objects into a second supposed truth. Primitive objects, arrays and collections do **not** become standalone content types. The inspector has `Preview / State / JSON Schema / History`. History shows event-linked additions, deletions and changed values for a content type or its canonical sources. Selection/configuration changes and direct local JSON edits are not labelled simulation events. An older selected State is read-only; the latest State remains directly editable.\n\n**Navigation:** separate top-level `Architecture A / Architecture B` (not two side-by-side architecture windows), each with its own Screens and panel positions. On a fresh workspace four sample screens are available: `Обзор`, `Разбор изменений`, `Факты и связи`, `План и прогнозы`. Existing customized saved layouts are not silently modified to insert new example screens: create windows via `+ Окно`, filter content using the search field, or use **Reset** (resets content as well) to load the fresh examples.\n\n**Workspace behavior:** any number of windows/screens; tabs; responsive content warnings; window geometry swapping; live drag with mouse-wheel and edge scrolling; fit-on-drop with editable gap; drag focus/status. Content State remains when a window disappears. Typed singletons (e.g., events/plan/requirements/current) are per screen, not duplicated semantic facts.\n\n## Data scope and persistence\n\nThe example has one application under architectures A and B. They share `EXT-01`, an architecture-independent external signal. Their **authored illustrative** reactions and downstream requirements differ with recorded provenance; the runtime does not prove causality. Selecting Plan Step does not execute it or advance factual time. Forecasts, conditional route impacts and deadlines are not facts.\n\n- `src/workspace.ts`: layout, panes, typed registry and placement constraints.\n- `src/content.ts`: original simulation fixture + schemas + direct edit validation.\n- `src/history.ts`: archived factual snapshots, immutable PlanRevision BASE/lineage, historical projection and structural before/after differences.\n- `src/HistoryContent.tsx`: State History and PlanRevision selectors/read-only details.\n- `src/extraContent.ts`: new typed view/inspection State and schemas (projections; canonical Plan and Events remain elsewhere).\n- `src/DomainContent.tsx`, `src/AdditionalContent.tsx`: old and added renderers.\n- `src/App.tsx`: root A/B screen UI, picker/search and overlay inspector.\n- `src/windowDrag.ts`: pointer dragging, edge scrolling, fit-on-drop.\n- `tests/*.test.mjs`: data/schema, migration, layout and geometry tests.\n\nState is saved under `pt006-simulator-content-[A|B]-v5`. Previous simulator State `-v4` and `-v3` are upgraded in memory. Customized data and layouts are preserved; an untouched v4 example Plan receives the revised sample. Histories come from the prepared scenario, not an inferred log of imported local edits; customized imports are labelled accordingly. Layout stays under `pt006-simulator-layout-[A|B]-v3`, so existing user layouts remain intact. If upgrading a **generic pre-simulator** layout (`pt006-workspace-v2`), screens and window rectangles are retained but generic content placements are cleared, rather than silently relabelled as new domain truths. Earlier generic demo data is never reinterpreted as factual simulator events. Previous storage keys are not deleted.\n\n## Verification boundaries\n\nThis is a catalog completeness prototype, **not** a successful Stage A/B/C simulation acceptance test. Prepared event-linked snapshots support historical browsing of Requirements, CURRENT architecture, files, work and Plan; three archived PlanRevisions per branch retain BASE, forecasts and deadline changes. There is no interpreter for arbitrary events, automatic IF execution, automatically captured local-edit history or measured expected-completion engine; no route likelihood engine; no causal proof or measured cost estimator; no universal architecture ontology; no independent Evolution Map. JSON Schema checking is a simplified structural validator; cross-content reference integrity is not generally enforced. The authored fixtures include labels to avoid interpreting planned targets as actual effects.\n\nSee [current full review](PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md) and [remediation status](../PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md). `CONTENT_INVENTORY_REVIEW_2026-10-10.md` preserves the preceding inventory review, findings, user-review priorities, pending decisions and next-stage limitations.\n\nHistorical proposal/review snapshots, PT-005 and `wireframe_app.xml` remain outside this remediation. Current entry documents link to the independently versioned v5/r10 supplements.\n\n## Historical fixture walkthrough\n\n- Open Actual Events and Current State. Select A-01 (12 March): API does not exist and `src/booking.ts` is present. Select A-02: API and `src/api/booking.ts` appear; the old file is removed.\n- Select EXT-01: R-A3 is still absent. Select A-04: the signed-contract event reveals R-A3.\n- Use the panel-edge ↶ button or the global inspector's History tab to compare saved objects and values and open complete historical JSON.\n- In Plan, choose R0/R1/R2. The factual cursor and CURRENT do not move. Expand changes or the frozen BASE. B's corporate deadline changes from 30 April in R1 to 15 May in R2.\n- Impact History / Future keeps actual changes and future conditional impacts in separate sections.\n- A custom event without a matching archived snapshot displays an explicit unavailable-state message; latest data is never silently shown as a past snapshot.\n\nThese are working historical projections of an authored test scenario, not a general simulation engine.\n\nVerified on Windows: 60/60 model/geometry tests, TypeScript/Vite build, zero lint errors/warnings. An isolated headless Edge session verified historical file browsing, read-only past State, before/after display, revision selection without moving CURRENT, changed B deadlines and migration preserving customized content/layout. No browser runtime exceptions.","content":"# PT-006 · Architecture Simulator Workspace\n\nИтерация исправлений 2026-10-10 завершена технически. Реализованы P6R-PR-01A и P6R-PR-02–06.\n[Рабочий журнал](../PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md) содержит принятый состав, результаты и ограничения.\nОснования: [SC-001@v5-candidate](../../../SC-001_desired_architecture_simulator_scenario_v5_candidate.md), [r10 delta](../../../architecture_simulator_proposal_composition_v3a_candidate_r10_pt006_remediation.md), [GLOSSARY](../../../GLOSSARY.md).\nПолная Scenario/V3A composition остаётся candidate. Это прототип инвентаризации и подготовленной истории.\n\n## Запуск и проверки\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\alexa\\simulation\\prototypes\\PT-006\\workspace-shell\nnpm run dev -- --port 4196 --strictPort\nnpm test\nnpm run build\nnpm run lint\n```\n\nОткройте http://127.0.0.1:4196/ . После обновления исходников обновите страницу.\n\n## 18 видов и новый материал\n\n| Вид | Материал |\n|---|---|\n| Scenario / Context | Общий старт, внешние якоря, динамичность проекта, команда и инженерная среда |\n| Actual Events | Фактические события A/B; полная лента для навигации |\n| Current State | Известные требования, фактический CURRENT и файлы выбранного момента |\n| Requirement Model | Ненормализованные фактические требования; прогнозы не становятся фактом автоматически |\n| Architecture | ACTUAL и PLANNED выбираются в явном контексте; один ID может иметь разные версии |\n| Architecture Planning | Полная цель выбранного Step из выбранной PlanRevision |\n| Plan | Один Plan: Steps, другая плановая работа, зависимости, возможные события, ожидания и сроки |\n| Forecasts / Deadlines | Конкретные прогнозные требования, основания ожиданий маршрутов, оценка завершения отдельно от обещания |\n| Planned Change Axes | Направление, значимость, горизонт, основание и исторический пересмотр |\n| Actual Hot Paths | Наблюдавшиеся изменения, отдельно от прогнозных осей |\n| Evolution Impact | Влияние Step одного маршрута, отдельно от полного снимка |\n| Impact History / Future | Фактические architecture/file переходы и отдельные условные будущие impacts |\n| Evolution Fitness | Цель и контекст каждого подготовленного маршрута, миграция, соответствие Plan, отдельные затраты |\n| Implementation / Files | Фактическое дерево файлов и отдельные плановые эффекты |\n| Requirement / Implementation Trace | Собственные связи requirement–architecture–file, включая историю note |\n| Event / Entity Explorer | Событие, новые требования и связанные architecture/file изменения |\n| Cross-Architecture Comparison | Общий стимул и объяснённые последствия A/B; отдельные фактические cursors |\n| Work Dynamics / Hot Paths | Работа по цели, knowledge/contracts/dependencies, compatibility/rollout, ожидание, откат, эксперимент, feedback, autonomy, cost/time provenance и фактический исход срока |\n\nКаталог имеет Preview / State / JSON Schema / History. Каждый вид имеет собственный State.\nПроекции раскрывают канонические source State/Schema. Scenario и Trace имеют собственные факты; Trace History включает links.\nПри выборе архивной PlanRevision доступны её сохранённые данные в отдельном плановом контексте. CURRENT разрешается из фактического контекста.\nВыбор Step/маршрута/вкладки не является выполнением работы или фактическим событием.\nИсторический State доступен только для чтения. Прямые JSON-правки последнего State не создают событий.\n\n## Навигация и Workspace\n\nArchitecture A/B — отдельные ветки с отдельными Screens и геометрией окон.\nНа новом Workspace четыре примерных экрана: Обзор, Разбор изменений, Факты и связи, План и прогнозы.\nОкна, вкладки и данные независимы: закрытие окна сохраняет State. Typed singletons ограничены экраном.\nСохранённая пользовательская раскладка не заполняется новыми окнами автоматически. Используйте + Окно и поиск каталога.\nDrag, обмен геометрией, прокрутка колёсиком/краем и fit-on-drop с gap сохранены.\nReset сбрасывает и контент, и раскладку после явного подтверждения.\n\n## Данные и перенос\n\nКонтент: pt006-simulator-content-[A|B]-v6. Layout: pt006-simulator-layout-[A|B]-v3.\nv5/v4/v3 переносятся; старые ключи не удаляются. Старый payload под текущим v6 key также проходит перенос.\nНетронутый подготовленный пример получает новый материал. Выборы и геометрия сохраняются.\nИзменённые пользовательские факты и архивы не заменяются новым примером. Отсутствующий новый раздел обозначается как не заданный.\nАрхив импортированного случая помечается отдельно; история локальных правок не выдумывается.\nУже подготовленный v6 State восстанавливается без повторной замены данных.\nGeneric pre-simulator layout переносит Screens/rects, но не переименовывает generic content в факты симулятора.\n\nОдин Plan остаётся каноническим источником планового материала. Нет отдельной Evolution Map.\nПримитивные Object, Array, Collection и Calendar не являются дополнительными видами каталога.\nПредупреждения о неразрешённых refs видны в State editor; структурно корректный черновик можно сохранить.\n\n## Исторический пример\n\n- A-01: API отсутствует, есть src/booking.ts. A-02: появляется API и src/api/booking.ts; старый файл удалён.\n- EXT-01: R-A3 ещё не известно. A-04: подписанный договор раскрывает R-A3.\n- Plan R1: FORECAST онбординга, неопределённый IF CONTRACT и интеграционная ось.\n- Plan R2: ожидания и оси меняются по информации A-04/B-04. Это не переписывает R1.\n- B R1: обещание 30 апр, оценка 27 апр. B R2: обещание пересогласовано на 15 мая, оценка 18 мая.\n- B-05, 16 мая: отдельный фактический исход пропуска обещания. На B-04 этого факта нет.\n- Выбор старого Plan сохраняет CURRENT. ACTUAL CURRENT и одноимённый PLANNED target разрешаются отдельно.\n- Правка порядка live-ленты не меняет архивные знания A-02. Полная лента остаётся для навигации.\n- Неизвестное или изменённое архивное событие не получает чужой State; кнопка «К последнему State» доступна.\n- История показывает порядок Steps, собственные Trace links и фактические sources проекций.\n\n## Файлы реализации\n\n- content.ts: State, Schema, проверка формы и перенос.\n- material.ts: авторские контекстные примеры и дополнительные формы Plan/Work.\n- history.ts: архивы, PlanRevision/BASE, контексты снимков, историческое знание и diff.\n- extraContent.ts: собственные view State/Schema и source mappings.\n- DomainContent.tsx / AdditionalContent.tsx / MaterialContent.tsx: представления.\n- HistoryContent.tsx: исторические selectors и before/after.\n- references.ts: диагностика ссылок без общего запрета черновиков.\n- App.tsx: A/B, сохранение/восстановление, каталог и State editor.\n- workspace.ts / windowDrag.ts: геометрия и перенос окон.\n- tests/remediation.test.mjs: regressions и перенос v5/v6.\n\n## Подтверждённые проверки и границы\n\nФинальный HOST: 71/71 tests, TypeScript/Vite build и lint без предупреждений/ошибок.\nОсновной браузерный прогон: 144 поверхности каталога и 9 исторических срезов. Финальные изменения проверены точечно.\nПроверены одинаковые snapshot IDs в разных контекстах, архивные знания после reorder, ordered diff, own Trace history, sources, новые разделы, draft warnings и сохранение custom data/archive/layout.\nСнимки прогноз/обязательство, рабочих условий и затрат просмотрены при 1600×1050.\nВсе UI-прогоны использовали отдельные профили; пользовательский профиль не менялся. Исключений приложения не зарегистрировано.\n\nЭто authored fixture, не интерпретатор произвольных событий. IF не исполняется автоматически.\nДаты, вероятность, причины, работа и затраты — авторские утверждения с источниками, без калиброванного расчёта или общего score.\nНеизвестная численная стоимость не равна нулю. Просрочка устанавливается фактическим событием, а не прогнозной датой.\nПолная ссылочная целостность произвольного материала, no-guide UX и Stage A/B/C не подтверждены.\n\n[Исходный полный review](PT006_independent_content_review_2026-10-10.md) и CONTENT_INVENTORY_REVIEW_2026-10-10.md сохранены как история до исправлений.\nАктуальные статусы находятся в [журнале исправлений](../PT006_REMEDIATION_2026-10-10.md). PT-005, исторические планы/reviews и wireframe_app.xml не изменены. Git commit в рабочем репозитории не создавался.\n"}];
